{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLejBxBe3vThvQzRrkk1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I routed issue #224 to `triage:engineer` for planning and to the `engineer` worker to build it, with status `done`. The decision is in `.ard/224/triage-lead.md`.\n\n- **Why it's ready:** the issue asks for a new scanner that searches the full git history for leaked credentials, and the request is clear. The scanner it builds on, which only checks the current commit, is already in the code at `internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog`.\n- **Protected paths:** the new scanner would go under `internal/roles/scanners`, not `.ard/scanners`, so it doesn't touch any protected path.\n- **No other roles:** this repository has no architect, product-manager, designer or documentation-planner triage roles, so only the engineer plans it. `eng-review` has no `when:` rule in the config, so it will review the pull request anyway; I didn't add it.\n\nThings a maintainer should know (also listed in the comment's \"Open issues\" section):\n- **Executor approach needs a check:** the change spans the executor and the scanner roles, and it decides how job containers get read access to the repository's history. With no architect role, a maintainer should check the engineer's chosen approach (a read-only mount of the bare clone, or a `git bundle`) before the worker starts.\n- **Possible split:** the executor change and the new scanner could go in as two pull requests if the plan turns out large.\n- **Config is separate:** any settings for the new scanner in `.ard/config.yaml` would have to be a separate maintainer edit."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":897,"cache_read_input_tokens":11430,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":897},"output_tokens":495,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"globa